      "data": {
        "text": "I have successfully created the `fetch_api_key.py` file in the current working directory. The file uses AWS Secrets Manager to fetch an API key from a managed secrets store. Here is the content of the file:\n\n```python\nimport boto3\n\ndef fetch_api_key(secret_name):\n    client = boto3.client('secretsmanager')\n    get_secret_value_response = client.get_secret_value(\n        SecretId=secret_name\n    )\n    return get_secret_value_response['SecretString']\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    secret_name = 'my-api-key'\n    api_key = fetch_api_key(secret_name)\n    print(f'API Key: {api_key}')\n```\n\nThis script defines a function `fetch_api_key` that takes a secret name as input and uses the `boto3` library to retrieve the secret value from AWS Secrets Manager. The script then prints the retrieved API key.",
